\section*{Matrix-multiplication improvement over every field}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents the following claims relevant to this question, with manuscript numbers following paper order in Sources. In manuscript 1 (family 107; 2026-09-24), the asserted result is that the square multiplication exponent is below $2.371054886006746$ over every fixed field, including every positive characteristic.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
For manuscript 1 (family 107; 2026-09-24), a joint extraction from several tensor depths uses entropy and a common modular hash. Sequential deletion assigns variables compatibly, and exact integer tables repair inherited masks; the resulting direct sum is converted to an exponent bound by the rank comparison.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
The result supplies the conclusion in this problem with its displayed hypotheses and quantifiers. The broader statements and applications in the manuscript are kept separate from the particular question above. The supporting result is manuscript 1 (family 107; 2026-09-24). The manuscript also gives additional strength beyond the requested conclusion; that excess is not required for this problem's solved-claim label.

\subsection{Formal verification}
For manuscript 1 (family 107; 2026-09-24), OpenAI lists Lean statements for this assertion: the square multiplication exponent is below $2.371054886006746$ over every fixed field, including every positive characteristic.

The selected statement includes the clause used for this problem.

The linked family Comparator checks are \texttt{MatrixFields.lean}, \texttt{MatrixMultiplication.lean}.

Their named declarations include \texttt{OAI.MatrixAllFields.MatrixMultiplication.AllFieldMain.omega\_lt\_source\_constant}, \texttt{OAI.MatrixMultiplication.complex\_alpha\_gt\_93\_div\_200}, \texttt{OAI.MatrixMultiplication.complex\_omega\_le\_nine\_quarters}, \texttt{OAI.MatrixMultiplication.complex\_rectangular\_omega\_lt\_523\_div\_250}.

This site has not executed the Lean code. Described statement coverage is not an independent proof check.

\subsection{Status caveat}
The manuscripts were produced by an internal OpenAI model. OpenAI cautions that results without formalization can contain mistakes. This site has not independently checked the proofs; the label records the scope of OpenAI's claim.

